The resolution of each read-out channel was about 60 ps after slewing corrections. It was measured with cosmic rays and with RHIC beams, by comparing the vertex positions extracted from the T0 counters with the vertex distribution obtained from the other detectors.

The PHOBOS start detector is the most similar to the pVPD. The Z-position of installation is similar, the number of channels on each side is similar, and the same model of PMTs are used. The difference is that the PHOBOS start detector uses quartz radiators, compared to the plastic scintillators used in the pVPD.

