Before sliding the PMTs into the shells, the bases were attached. Figure 2.8 shows a base attached to a PMT. The circular edge of the base was wrapped with Kapton tape to electrically insulate it from the aluminum shell. Shown in Figure 2.9 is a PMT being slipped into a shell. Two pieces of foam tape (5 inch long and half inch wide) were attached around the PMT, making two rings, which serve as an elastic cushion between the PMT and the shell's inner surface.

